CVE-2026-78662: ssh: drop traffic on undecided channels

A channel registered in the mux's chanList is not usable until it is
established. A malicious peer could flood the channel's incomingRequests,
blocking the mux read loop and deadlocking the entire connection, or close an
outbound channel before confirming it. This adds an established flag (distinct
from the existing decided flag) so that handlePacket drops every packet other
than the open confirmation/failure until the channel is properly confirmed or
accepted, without blocking and without tearing down the connection.

Backport of upstream commit a6cdac60840750226b15617ac8858be44361b36b.

Fixes CVE-2026-78662
Fixes golang/go#81316

